## Summary

SkyPlan does not require an account. It uses a city you choose or your device location to provide weather forecasts. If you choose to connect a calendar, SkyPlan reads selected event details from your device solely to compare events with the forecast; those calendar details are not sent to SkyPlan’s servers or weather providers.

SkyPlan sends location search terms, city names, ZIP/postal codes, or coordinates to its weather proxy. The proxy forwards the needed location query to WeatherAPI and temporarily caches weather responses. The app also makes direct requests to NASA GIBS, OpenStreetMap, and WeatherAPI map-tile services for the satellite and precipitation-map features. Optional route and traffic actions open Google Maps outside SkyPlan.

We do not sell personal information, use advertising, or use a dedicated in-app analytics or crash-reporting SDK in the current version of SkyPlan.

